4
00:00:12.761 --> 00:00:16.731
Today we learn about Understanding Phishing. Let's go!

5
00:00:17.673 --> 00:00:21.140
Phishing. Say it with me. Phishing!

6
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.865
Fake email. Say it with me. Fake email!

7
00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:36.498
Trick users. Say it with me. Trick users!

8
00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:44.650
Steal information. Say it with me. Steal information!

9
00:00:48.166 --> 00:00:52.532
Suspicious link. Say it with me. Suspicious link!

10
00:00:56.046 --> 00:00:59.980
Impersonate. Say it with me. Impersonate!

11
00:01:03.464 --> 00:01:07.655
Scam attempt. Say it with me. Scam attempt!

12
00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:15.560
Verify sender. Say it with me. Verify sender!

13
00:01:19.043 --> 00:01:27.471
Phishing uses a fake email to trick users into revealing information. I stay alert for a suspicious link and verify the sender before clicking.

14
00:01:27.521 --> 00:01:30.712
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:31.773 --> 00:01:37.167
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:37.217 --> 00:01:38.532
Trick users!

17
00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:44.915
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:44.965 --> 00:01:46.262
Scam attempt!

19
00:01:47.339 --> 00:01:54.511
Did you know? The word 'phishing' is a play on the word 'fishing', since scammers are 'fishing' for your personal information!

20
00:01:54.561 --> 00:01:56.590
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:06.482
Think and answer. What is one sign that an email might be a phishing attempt?

22
00:02:06.532 --> 00:02:07.682
Great answer!

23
00:02:08.971 --> 00:02:14.260
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
